    "status": "accepted",
    "owner_role": "scientific_authority",
    "accepted_scope": "Fixture-local executable composition from resolved YYZ scientific components through two consecutive lookup-composed FrozenIntervals, a committed-observation altitude guidance law, a pitch-moment controller, ideal zero-delay moment realization, two atomic rigid-and-mass commits, committed-boundary evaluation, a sealed terminal observation, a frozen mission result and structured diagnostics for three pre-commit failures.",
    "source_policy": "The source is a fixture input with explicit stable identities and component bindings. It does not define the product MissionSource schema or invoke a product Compiler, Plan, Session or Artifact runtime.",
    "numeric_policy": "REF-YYZ-FROZEN-INTERVAL-001 supplies the accepted interval formulas. Tick 1 recomputes air-data, aero lookup, dimensionalization, propulsion, mass projection and Closure from the newly committed rigid state and mass. Each interval uses one classical RK4 base step; 1/2/4/8 substep results expose fourth-order self-convergence.",
    "tolerance_policy": "Formula and state comparisons retain 2e-12 absolute/relative tolerances. The derived convergence-ratio comparison uses 5e-4 absolute tolerance because it divides successive O(dt^5) differences; every independently computed ratio must still exceed the 12-fold fourth-order qualification threshold.",
    "reuse_policy": "REF-YYZ-TWO-INTERVAL-MASS-COMMIT-001 contributes the accepted atomic commit time relation. Its independent supplied-force trajectory is not substituted for the lookup-composed trajectory.",
    "termination_policy": "Metrics read committed samples only. Inclusive AtGrid any-of predicates use higher integer priority and ascending predicate_id tie-breaking. The terminal observation seals before the mission result freezes.",
    "guidance_control_policy": "At each committed boundary, +I-z position and velocity feed a fixture-local altitude PD law. Its bounded pitch command and the committed pure-pitch attitude/rate feed a bounded pitch-moment PD controller. A fixture-local ideal zero-delay transform realizes the current-cycle command as a +B-y moment contribution held in the following FrozenInterval. This two-interval qualification establishes formula, sign, saturation and causal timing only; it makes no stability or overshoot claim.",
    "diagnostic_policy": "The fixture emits immutable diagnostic facts, a separate qualification decision and a failed step outcome for stale Closure timing, a split rigid/mass candidate set and an aero model-domain violation. Codes are stable inside this fixture and do not allocate entries in a production DiagnosticCode registry.",
    "excluded": [
      "canonical YYZ mission, qualification thresholds, assets and production tolerances",
      "canonical guidance/controller tuning, allocator, control-surface mapping, actuator dynamics and closed-loop stability or overshoot claims",
      "product MissionSource, Compiler, PlanProofRecord, Session, DiagnosticRecord, DiagnosticCode registry, ObservationBatch, RunOutcome and Artifact contracts",
      "continuous event location, partial-time commit, persistence, evidence durability and R1-R8 runtime capability"
    ]
  },
